## GIT OPERATIONS - FULLY AUTOMATED

**All git operations execute automatically (see `CORE-AUTOMATION.mdc`):**

- `git add` → Automatic (no user approval needed)
- `git commit` → Automatic (no user approval needed)
- `git push` → Automatic (no user approval needed)
- `git merge` → Automatic (no user approval needed)
- `git branch` (create/delete) → Automatic (no user approval needed)

**Automation guarantees:**
- Required safety checks (validation, formatting, etc.) still run before and after commits/pushes
- Corrections are applied automatically
- Status updates remain informational: report what happened and what comes next, never ask for permission

**Mandatory chat updates:**
- Immediately after executing any git command, send an informational chat update summarizing:
  - The action that was just performed
  - The branch(es) involved
  - Resulting commit hashes or PR identifiers when applicable
  - Next automated step (if any)

