  - <file1>
  - <file2>
  ...

PUSH STATUS: ✅ SUCCESS / ❌ FAILED
VERIFICATION: GitHub link or manual verification instructions
NEXT ACTION: <validation, merge, cleanup, etc.>

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
```

**WHY THIS IS MANDATORY**:
- Enables cross-verification on GitHub.com later
- Provides audit trail for all commits
- Helps debug if commits don't appear on GitHub
- Essential for team coordination
- Required for compliance tracking

**WHEN TO DISPLAY**:
- ✅ After EVERY `git commit` command (including auto-commits during merges or rebase)
- ✅ After EVERY `git push` command
- ✅ After automated pushes (auto-fix loops, validation reruns)
- ✅ After merge commits that land on `beta`
- ✅ After PR merges that push to beta
- ✅ When push or commit fails (include error details and remediation steps)

**NEVER SKIP THIS** - This is a mandatory reporting requirement for all git operations.

